data.content:
Here are the three EF Core 10 breaking changes affecting your code and how to fix them:

---

## 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — now accepts a regular lambda

The API changed from `Expression<Func<...>>` to `Action<...>`. Your expression tree construction code won't compile. Replace with a simple lambda:

```csharp
// .NET 10 fix
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

No more manual `Expression.Call`/`Expression.Lambda` needed.

---

## 2. Complex type column names — uniquified & full-path nested

Two changes apply:

- **Duplicate property names** (e.g., `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street`): columns are now auto-uniquified with a numeric suffix. This generates a rename migration.
- **Nested complex types** (e.g., `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City`): column name changes from `BillingAddress_City` to `Payment_BillingAddress_City`.

**Fix:** Pin the old names explicitly to avoid a breaking migration:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, sa =>
        sa.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, ba =>
        ba.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street"));
});

// For nested complex types:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, p =>
        p.ComplexProperty(pay => pay.BillingAddress, ba =>
            ba.Property(a => a.City).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City")));
});
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

Methods now require an additional `string logCommandText` parameter:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)   // ← new parameter (redacted SQL for logging)
    {
        // Use logCommandText for safe logging (constants may be redacted)
        // Use command.CommandText for actual SQL
    }
}
```

Add this parameter to **all** methods in the interface (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.).
